cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper."
title: "The geometry of single-cell foundation models: what they inherit, what they add, and what shapes it"
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous authors"
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and results for a study of representational geometry in single-cell foundation models.
  Cell-level geometry is shown to be a re-description of the model's input; gene-vocabulary facts
  such as chromosome membership are shown to be genuinely learned and causally used; and a mechanism
  is given for what determines the shape a representation takes.
